-- Before downloading the django software. we have to create virtual environment.

-- venv ensures that the entire system is not containing the django software so that if there is any mismatch of the django version b/w 2 different projects then they will not get effected.

-- to create venv we have to follow the below steps 
1. create a project director.
2. Run "python -m venv venvName" -- creates venv in the director. 
3. Activate the venv by running the command "venvName\Scripts\activate" 
4. install django inside the venv.
"pip install django"
5. To see the installed django software run command -- "pip list"
6. If you run command -- "django-admin --version"

---------------------------------------

TO CREATE DJANGO PROJECT FOLLOW THE BELOW STEPS : 

1. Run command "django-admin startproject projectName"
2. To run the application we have to go to app directory then run command 
"python manage.py runserver"

NOTE : 
project -- application that we are working on.

app -- a module that belongs to the application.

manage.py -- helps to run our application

folder with the projectName -- main folder.

settings.py -- Here we configure the application. Encryp, Decrypt, database credentials

urls.py -- Here we map the requests and responses. 

-----------------------------------------